-- 143_play_input_and_capture.surql -- the first human session: the XInput index-1 defect that silenced all
-- directions, and the measured proof that the frame stall is the CAPTURE and not the engine.
-- SUPERGUN ENGINE lane, 2026-09-04 (odd seeds). Doc: mvc-live-skins-quarters/docs/RECEIPT-RUNNER-PLAY.md add. A
-- Idempotent and replayable; explicit edge ids; additive fields only on findings owned by earlier seeds.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:play_session_20260904 SET kind='capture', strength='runtime',
  ref='Tris 600-frame --play session, arc-built stage-9 anchor, 2026-09-04; plus rr_runner --pad-probe on the same machine',
  note='First input frame 17, first px change frame 277. Every pad word in the session had a low byte of 00, so no direction ever reached the sim. --pad-probe then reported XInput connected on user index mask 0x2.';

UPSERT finding:play_xinput_index_defect SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-04',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='All direction input was silently dropped: the controller was on XInput user index 1 and padRead polled only index 0',
  statement='rr_runner --pad-probe reports XInput controllers connected on user index mask 0x2, i.e. user index 1. The first padRead polled index 0 only, received ERROR_DEVICE_NOT_CONNECTED and fell through to the keyboard, so the gamepad was invisible for the whole 600-frame session. The bits that did appear (0x0800, 0x2000, 0x4000) are exactly keyboard A, S and D under the documented map; 0x8000, 0x1000 and 0x200 (Z, X, C on the row below) never appeared, which is consistent with a hand resting on the home row rather than a controller. Three separate bugs each drop direction input with no error: (1) the XInput branch RETURNED EARLY so with any controller connected the keyboard was never read; (2) only user index 0 was polled so a pad on 1..3 contributed nothing -- this is the one that bit; (3) the left-stick deadzone was 12000, 37 percent of full scale, against the XInput standard of 7849.',
  fix='All four user indices are polled, the keyboard is ALWAYS OR-ed in rather than reached only as a fallback, the deadzone is 7849, and the raw xiMask / wButtons / LX / LY / kbBits are recorded in g_padRaw so a session can be audited instead of guessed at. New --pad-probe N mode exercises the input path alone with no image, no anchor and no tick, and states whether any direction was seen.';

UPSERT finding:play_steering_needs_a_direction_bit SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-04',
  title='A human-caused move detector that accepts any input can fire on an assist call and read as steering',
  statement='The first detector announced FIRST HUMAN-CAUSED MOVE on pad 000800, which is A2 alone. An assist call is not locomotion, and the px slide from -134 to -495 that followed under an unchanging pad is animation displacement or pushback rather than the player walking. The headline is now gated on PAD_DIRS (0xF0): rr_runner reports FIRST INPUT, FIRST DIRECTION and STEERING PROVEN separately, and when no direction ever appears it states that inputs reached the sim but steering is unproven. This is the same failure shape as py idle bob: a signal that reads like the claim you want but is generated by something else.';

UPSERT finding:play_stall_is_the_capture SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-04',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The play-loop frame stall is the per-tick harvest, not the simulation',
  statement='Tris session: 57.9 fps, per-frame work p50 8.13 ms but p99 34.36 ms and max 97.74 ms, with frame indices skipping in the log, while the tick itself stayed at p50 0.164 ms and max 0.749 ms. Cheap discriminator, 600 frames per arm, same anchor and build, nobody at the controls: with the per-tick harvest INLINE, 58.4 fps and per-frame work p50 10.357, p99 34.099, max 58.054 ms; with the harvest OFF, 60.1 fps and p50 1.164, p99 2.002, max 4.730 ms. p99 falls 17 times and the worst frame 12 times, and the loop holds a clean 60 Hz. The harvest is a RECORDING concern that does not belong on the frame thread.',
  action='--play-harvest off is now the default for --play and play_session.py requires --record to enable it, with the cost stated at the point of use. NO memcmp optimisation was attempted: establishing the discriminator first settles the question on its own. Moving the harvest to a ring drained by a second thread is the real fix and is NOT done.';

UPSERT finding:playable_loop_chain_closes SET
  first_session_note='2026-09-04: Tris ran 600 frames -- first input frame 17, first px change frame 277, so a human input demonstrably reaches the real frame function from his own arc. STEERING remains UNPROVEN: no direction bit was set in the whole session because of the XInput index defect (finding:play_xinput_index_defect). The 60 Hz claim holds only with the harvest off (finding:play_stall_is_the_capture).';

RELATE finding:play_xinput_index_defect->cites:p143_xi_run->source:play_session_20260904;
RELATE finding:play_xinput_index_defect->cites:p143_xi_tool->source:tool_play_session;
RELATE finding:play_steering_needs_a_direction_bit->cites:p143_dir_run->source:play_session_20260904;
-- the schema ASSERT on finding.status requires at least one cites->source of strength 'code'/'reproduction'
RELATE finding:play_steering_needs_a_direction_bit->cites:p143_dir_tool->source:tool_play_session;
RELATE finding:play_stall_is_the_capture->cites:p143_cap_run->source:play_session_20260904;
RELATE finding:play_stall_is_the_capture->cites:p143_cap_tool->source:tool_play_session;
